
nomlib provides CMake import targets:

    find_package(nomlib CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main
      PRIVATE
      nomlib-actions
      nomlib-audio
      nomlib-core
      nomlib-file
      nomlib-graphics
      nomlib-gui
      nomlib-math
      nomlib-ptree
      nomlib-serializers
      nomlib-system
    )

    If you need to force a particular linkage, request the `static` or `shared`
    component when calling find_package:

        find_package(nomlib CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS static)

    When neither component is requested, nomlib follows `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS` by
    picking shared targets when available and falling back to static targets.

NOTE: The installed `nomlib.pc` pkg-config file is supplied as-is by the
upstream build system and is currently incomplete / assumed broken. It leaks
absolute paths, uses semicolon separators, and lists vendored dependencies
that are not resolvable by pkg-config. Use the CMake import targets above
instead.

